{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>That came after them into the sea.</b> It is the practice of the Torah scrolls (ס״ת) that six stand at the heads of the columns (ששה בריש דפין), and the mnemonic is בי״ה שמ״ו. And these are they: ב'ראשית, י'הודה אתה יודוך, ה'באים אחריהם, ש'מור ושמעת, מ'צא שפתיך, ו'אעידה בם. And it may be that there is a reason for this, that it is an allusion to the renewal of the world — that the Holy One, blessed be He, rides upon the desert plains (ערבות), in the manner of what is written (Psalms 68:5): ״סולו לרוכב בערבות ביה שמו״. And observe how He completed the allusion of the ה״א of בי״ה in the matter of the Sea, where Moses mentioned there ״עזי וזמרת יה״, and therefore he mentioned ״מי כמוכה״ twice with this ה״א, and the added ה״א in the first ״מי כמוכה״ is the last one in the Name and it is the last of the sefirot, and it is the angel of Elohim whom Scripture mentioned concerning him ״וילך מאחריהם״, and likewise here, ״הבאים אחריהם בים״. For the salvation of the Sea was through him. And according to what the Sages, of blessed memory (רז״ל), expounded on ״בהבראם בה׳ בראם״ — one said: in the merit of Abraham (בזכות אברהם) — you will find that the secondary letters to the letters בי״ה שמ״ו spell אברהם, and the addition of the ו״ו is to make known that the six (ו׳) extremities of the world were created in his merit; and Scripture testifies that the world was built upon the attribute of lovingkindness, as is said (Psalms 89): ״כי אמרתי עולם חסד יבנה״, and it is written (Micah 7): ״חסד לאברהם״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The phrase ששה בריש דפין refers to six words that, by scribal tradition, must begin a new column in a Torah scroll; the mnemonic בי״ה שמ״ו gives their initial letters."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:12.191851833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}